# Persistent Marshstalker: turn 1 Black Lotus pays for Entomb (fetching the Marshstalker into the graveyard), four Dark Rituals
# and a Typhoid Rats; Lotus, Entomb, the Marshstalker and the four Rituals make seven cards in the graveyard (threshold). On
# turn 7 the Rats attacks, the trigger (functioning from the graveyard, CR 113.6m) asks for {2}{B}, paid from three Swamps, and
# the Marshstalker returns as a new object tapped and attacking (CR 508.4): 3 base +1 for the other Rat = 4, plus the Rats's 1
# = 5 combat damage, 20 - 5 = 15. The pool is empty right after the payment: {2}{B} exactly. Three Swamps come one a turn (turns 3, 5, 7), so no mana is left from turn 1.

